 seven forms of one family on separate cards. Mix the cards. Rebuild the sequence from 1st to 7th order and read it aloud. Move from shape to use Model → trace → copy → cover → write → read. Keep the sound and the written form together. ☐ Write each -wa form five times. ☐ Say ኳ and ሏ aloud. ☐ Create one short phrase containing ኳ or ሏ. UNIT 1 • ማንበብ እና መጻፍ • Reading & Writing Workshop Word checkpoint ደብዳቤ • ቤት • ቡና • ሻይ • ካርታ • መኪና Practical activity: teach-back Teach one family to a partner for 60 seconds. Your partner reads it back without looking at your page. ☐ Read every word aloud. ☐ Underline the Fidel you recognize. ☐ Write three words from memory. UNIT 1 • ፊደል ማረጋገጫ • Fidel Checkpoint Figure 2. Review the seven-order pattern before the checkpoint. Original AmharicAI illustration. Challenge A • Complete the pattern ለ, ሉ, ______, ላ, ______, ል, ______ Challenge B • Read ቤት • ቡና • ሻይ • ካርታ • መኪና Challenge C • Mini-teaching task Choose one family and explain its seven-order sequence to another learner. Then ask the learner to write it from memory. ☐ I can recognize seven orders. ☐ I can distinguish key consonants. ☐ I can copy short words. ☐ I can explain the practice routine. UNIT 2 • ሰላምታ እና መሰናበት • Greetings & Leave-Taking Learning goal Greet, respond, and leave politely in common social situations. Figure 3. Unit 2 visual language guide. Original AmharicAI educational illustration."
